D1
~
~
0 0 6509
D3
~
~
0 0 6507
S
#6509
The Cavern~
   Powerful internal pressures squeezed that ocean bed like a crumpled rug to
form the Northern Hills.  As the rain fell on these hills, so it began to
dissolve the weaknesses in the rock, little by little widening cracks, eating
into softer parts, turning into rivulets and streams.  Deep in the earth they
became the River Axe.  It broke through fissures in the great blocks of
limestone, swirled around huge beds of the conglomerate, and worked away to
enlarge the caverns, always seeking new shafts and tunnels down into the earth
and eventually back into the sunlight and the distant sea.    
~
