#6531
Cathedral Cavern~
   This is one of the most famous caverns in the history of cave diving.  It is
100 feet high, its green water 70 feet deep, its vast walls red with iron oxide
and shining with "flowstone" stalactite formations.  High on one wall is a
beautiful "curtain" stalactite.  And, most valuable of all for the divers,
there is a wide curve of mud bank above the green water, enough for men and
supplies to remain dry.    
~
